    "result_text": "All 276 tests pass, including the new `Cp14Tests`. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented a per-city owner cap that rejects creating an owner once their city already contains 8 owners, responding with **400 Bad Request**. Following the existing OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (mirroring the daily-limit rule), I added:\n\n1. **`CheckCityOwnerCap`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 counts existing owners in the new owner's city (case-insensitive) and throws `CityOwnerCapException` when the count is already \u2265 8. Runs after `NormalizeCity` so it compares against the canonical city spelling, and before `SaveOwner` so an over-cap owner never reaches the store.\n\n2. **`CityOwnerCapException`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 a checked exception mapping to 400.\n\n3. **`CityOwnerCapExceptionHandler`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail`, matching the daily-limit handler.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.CityOwnerCapException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted a `checkCityCap` step into `owners.POST.yml` between the daily-limit check and membership assignment, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nThe 9th owner in a city is now rejected with 400, and all prior rules and tests remain green.",
